ct49CxSXc-RHzG4IgIMqF5_hBGBlVG7Sbzr0rdM-0yZlTbHI1zSVOTigcpHkGBaTs0_FUccfVqOjCSHIzJlmoduk2iw58wIp97XJES-NltvvcR86s5cXGwEiPUa18Bc_h_ZyTVbIss-C9BLAvONWZqFRa9GlihSLKKnTxc8pl596a9Q1Kcc43PA=="}, {"type": "message", "id": "msg_05e6ec7028a81c3e016ad77db8406c819a8518ec1d1193d538", "metadata": {"turn_id": "01a159c2-e2ca-7870-a53b-80a82f0cd751"}, "internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough": {"create_time": 1792507320.2529986, "turn_id": "01a159c2-e2ca-7870-a53b-80a82f0cd751"}, "role": "assistant", "status": "completed", "content": [{"type": "output_text", "text": "At dawn, the river wakes before the town. Mist gathers above its dark surface, turning bends and islands into unfinished thoughts. Beneath the haze, water moves with quiet purpose, carrying leaves, silt, reflections, and the memory of distant rain. A heron stands in the shallows, patient as a stone, while minnows scatter beneath its shadow.\n\nBy midmorning, the river becomes a road for light. Sunbeams break into bright fragments, and every ripple catches a different sky. Children lean over the bank to launch twigs, racing them toward the bridge. Their laughter joins the calls of birds and the steady hush of current against reeds. For a moment, nobody asks where the water came from or where it will go.\n\nYet the river remembers every place it has touched. It gathers snowmelt from mountains, springs from hidden valleys, and runoff from streets. It passes farms, factories, forests, and homes, linking their choices in one moving story. What one community pours into its waters may travel far beyond its own horizon. The river therefore offers beauty, but also a plain responsibility: what we release eventually belongs to someone else.\n\nAt evening, the current turns copper beneath the setting sun. The bridge lights appear one by one, trembling in the darkening reflection. Night does not stop the river. It continues under stars, around sleeping roots, toward wetlands, lakes, and the sea. Its destination matters, but so does its motion. The river teaches that persistence need not be loud. It can be patient, changing, and faithful, shaping stone through countless ordinary moments. To stand beside it is to feel time moving, not away, but onward. In its endless passage, the river carries more than water; it carries warnings, possibilities, and a promise that renewal begins wherever attention meets care and hands choose wisely before the next dawn.\n\n1", "annotations": [], "logprobs": []}], "phase": "final_answer"}], "error": null, "incomplete_details": null, "tool_choice": "auto", "parallel_tool_calls": false, "prompt_cache_key": "01a159c2-d110-7ad2-8199-682dcc6a7f72", "prompt_cache_retention": "24h", "prompt_cache_options": {"ttl": "30m", "mode": "implicit", "comparison_response_id": "resp_05e6ec7028a81c3e016ad77dac4144819a880266449ca430eb"}, "prompt_cache_diagnostics": {"type": "unavailable"}, "text": {"format": {"type": "text"}, "verbosity": "low"}, "top_p": 0.98, "top_logprobs": 0, "temperature": 1.0, "reasoning": {"effort": "medium", "context": "all_turns", "summary": null, "mode": "standard"}, "usage": {"input_tokens": 20590, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 19584, "cache_write_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 1232, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 849}, "total_tokens": 21822, "attribution": {"items": {"amsg_01a159c2-e7ea-7060-bae1-adcc8619cda8": {"input_tokens": 74, "cached_tokens": 0, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 0}, "at_17070085-4613-50b4-94a1-39df5f3e42b8": {"input_tokens": 6908, "cached_tokens": 6908, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 0}, "ctc_05e6ec7028a81c3e016ad77daedde4819a846383414ce240fd": {"input_tokens": 406, "cached_tokens": 0, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 0}, "ctco_01a159c3-017e-7480-b5c3-c84e17c97bbf": {"input_tokens": 39, "cached_tokens": 0, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 0, "content": [{"input_tokens": 20, "cached_tokens": 0, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 0}, {"input_tokens": 19, "cache